{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:42` sets `BUGFIX_SIZE_THRESHOLD_NON_TEST_LINES = 150`. On Gerrit only, a change whose trailer resolves to a `bug` and whose diff exceeds 150 non-test lines must carry an acceptable plan-review attestation or the bot votes `LLM-Review -1` (`bugfix_size_gate.py:248-322`; docs `docs/plan-review-gate.md:1058`). A fix at or under the floor is never asked for a plan.\n\nMeasured by `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --rev-range origin/main` (no `--since` exists, so this is all of `origin/main`):\n\n- 644 bug-fix commits; 105 over the floor = 16.3% escalation.\n- \"This fix later introduced a bug\" is labellable from the store's `caused_by` field (`rebar.metrics.blame.derive_caused_by`, aggregated by `bug_trends.caused_by_fan_in`, 70 culprits): 22 of the 644 name one.\n- Size floor catches 10 of 22. Repeat-fix signal (a non-test file touched by >=2 other bug-fix commits on the base branch in the prior 7 days) catches 12 of 22 at 34.8% escalation (224/644). Union: 14 of 22 at 39.0%.\n- Under the floor today: `8d862d1058` (bug `7084-4e33-e698-42dd`) is 127 non-test lines.\n\nPure git history plus ticket type — no path lists, no CI provider required (portability).\n\n## Approach\nNew module `src/rebar/llm/code_review/repeat_fix.py`: `REPEAT_FIX_WINDOW_DAYS = 7`, `REPEAT_FIX_MIN_PRIOR = 2`, `repeat_fix_escalates(paths, *, repo_root, base_ref, at) -> tuple[bool, list[str]]` (verdict + the priors the teaching finding names). Per non-test path it walks `git log --no-merges --since/--until <path>` on the base branch, counting commits whose message resolves to a `bug` ticket.\n\n`apply_bugfix_size_gate` gains this order, which preserves the other pinned exemptions: (1) extract non-test paths, empty -> return with no reads; (2) escalate if `non_test_lines > 150` OR `repeat_fix_escalates(...)`, else return; (3) resolve ticket, require `ticket_type == \"bug\"`, classify attestation — unchanged.\n\n## Constraints\n- **The `review-plan` mirror is a no-op; NOT in scope.** `orchestrator.bug_blast_radius_escalates` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:191-211`) already returns True for a bug whose `file_impact` names ANY non-test path, which every repeat-fix bug does. The only bugs a mirror could newly escalate have empty/test-only `file_impact`, where the predicate cannot fire either. Its call sites `orchestrator.py:245` and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:127` stay unchanged; the docs edit records this so it is not re-proposed.\n- **A pinned invariant changes deliberately.** `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:304` (`test_under_threshold_diff_never_reads_the_store`) patches `ticket_for_commit_message`, `_load_ticket_state`, `classify_plan_review_attestation` to raise and asserts an under-floor diff leaves the verdict untouched — but the predicate must run on under-floor diffs. Rewrite it to the surviving invariant: an under-floor diff with no non-test files, or no repeat-fix hit, performs no attestation classification. `test_test_only_diff_is_exempt_even_when_huge` (`:320`) must pass unchanged.\n- **`flagged` keeps meaning the size floor alone.** `--check-planning-corpus` (`scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py:180-191`) asserts the flagged set equals `ADJUDICATED_SUBSTANTIVE` exactly, so the repeat-fix verdict is a NEW field beside `flagged`, never folded into it.\n- **Additive coverage keys only.** `coverage[\"bugfix_size_gate\"]` gains `escalation_reason` (`size`/`repeat-fix`/`size+repeat-fix`) and `repeat_fix_priors` as NEW keys, so the consumers need no edit: `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py:202-215` (imports `bucket_for_verdict`, `classify_plan_review_attestation`, `ticket_for_commit_message` by name) and `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:345-347`.\n- **Reuse the resolver.** Commit->ticket resolution exists at `bugfix_size_gate.py:138-151` and `metrics/blame.py:171`; call the former, do not add a third copy.\n- **Patchable by name.** Reach the predicate through a module-level name in `bugfix_size_gate`, so the existing string-keyed `monkeypatch.setattr(bsg, \"<name>\", ...)` sites (`test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py:210-224`, `:308-310`, no `raising=False`) can neutralise it.\n- **Ratchets / fail-open.** `apply_bugfix_size_gate` scores C901 9 of 15 and the module is 322 of 800 lines, so extract the predicate evaluation into a helper. A git failure yields no escalation and no exception.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/repeat_fix.py` (new); `bugfix_size_gate.py`; `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` (add `--repeat-fix` and `--labels-from-caused-by`, importing the shipped predicate so the script cannot drift); `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (the section at `:1058` — there is no \"escalation section\" in that file); `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`; `tests/unit/test_bugfix_repeat_fix_1dd5.py` (new).\n\nReviewed, NOT changed: `orchestrator.py`, `workflow_ops.py`, `test_bug_blast_radius_escalation_ad0d.py`, `review_bot/retrigger.py`, `code_review/finalize.py`, `metrics/blame.py`.\n\n## Testing\nFixture repo built in-test, not this repo's history. Escalates: two prior bug-trailer commits inside 7 days on a 20-line fix. Does not: one prior fix; two 8 days back; priors resolving to a non-bug ticket or to nothing; merge commits; a test-only diff (which also reads nothing). The floor still escalates alone; a git failure fails open.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Predicate + parameters ship in their own module. `grep -c \"REPEAT_FIX_WINDOW_DAYS\\|REPEAT_FIX_MIN_PRIOR\\|def repeat_fix_escalates\" src/rebar/llm/code_review/repeat_fix.py` prints `3`. Today the file is absent (exit 2).\n- [ ] New unit tests pass. `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_repeat_fix_1dd5.py -q` exits 0. Today pytest exits 4.\n- [ ] An under-floor repeat-fix is escalated. `tests/unit/test_bugfix_repeat_fix_1dd5.py::test_repeat_fix_escalates_an_under_floor_bug_fix` asserts `verdict[\"coverage\"][\"bugfix_size_gate\"][\"escalation_reason\"] == \"repeat-fix\"`. Today an under-floor diff writes no `coverage` entry (`bugfix_size_gate.py:262-263`).\n- [ ] Existing gate behaviour preserved. `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py tests/unit/test_bug_blast_radius_escalation_ad0d.py -q` exits 0 (pinning; passes today, with the one test rewritten as above).\n- [ ] Backtest emits the repeat-fix verdict from the shipped predicate. `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --rev-range HEAD~200..HEAD --repeat-fix --out /tmp/bt.json` exits 0 and `python -c \"import json; c=json.load(open('/tmp/bt.json'))['commits']; assert c and all('repeat_fix' in r for r in c)\"` exits 0. Today `--repeat-fix` is unrecognised (exit 2) and rows carry only `commit`/`ticket`/`non_test_lines`/`flagged`.\n- [ ] Backtest labels from the store and reports recall per predicate. `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --rev-range origin/main --repeat-fix --labels-from-caused-by --out /tmp/bt_full.json` exits 0 and prints labelled-recall + escalation rate per predicate (2026-08-21: 22 labelled; floor 10/22 at 16.3%, repeat-fix 12/22 at 34.8%, union 14/22 at 39.0%). Today `--labels-from-caused-by` is unrecognised (exit 2). The command recomputes its own figures, so the criterion is that the summary exists and its floor row reconciles with `--check-planning-corpus`, not that the digits are frozen.\n- [ ] `flagged` still means the floor alone. `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --check-planning-corpus` exits 0 (pinning; the guard that the new field sits beside `flagged`).\n- [ ] Docs record the predicate and why `review-plan` is not mirrored. `grep -c \"repeat-fix\" docs/plan-review-gate.md` prints >= `2`. Today `0`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787371038743031001,"uuid":"bd93ca72-69d9-4404-86e5-d0894c56a20c"}